OL,3,GNEWSATruckloads of debris wash ashore
OL,4,Afrom fishing boat that smashed onto
OL,5,Arocks
OL,6,
OL,7,FSince then, fishing boxes, pallets and
OL,8,Fparts of the vessel itself have been
OL,9,Fwashing up along the coastline,
OL,10,Fbuffeted about by recent storms. Items
OL,11,Falso include personal belongings such
OL,12,Fas welly boots, thought to have
OL,13,Fbelonged to members of the crew.
OL,15,FThose picking up the debris at Rackwick
OL,16,FBay told the BBC they will be finding
OL,17,Fparts of the wreckage for "months or
OL,18,Fyears to come".
